== B9: the two columns of the exclusion table
  alpha = 1.000: one-sided +alpha95 40.66 um, two-sided |alpha95| 38.63 um
  alpha = 1.333: one-sided +alpha95 37.68 um, two-sided |alpha95| 35.79 um
  alpha = 2.667: one-sided +alpha95 31.69 um, two-sided |alpha95| 30.23 um
  -> the published 38.6 um (|alpha| = 1) and 30 um (alpha = 8/3) are reproduced by the |alpha95| column;
     the note's 37.7 um is the +alpha95 column at 4/3 (more conservative than the |alpha95| 35.8 um).

== B10: readings of the withdrawn claim
  squeezed mode, r = 100.0: aspect e^(2r) = 10^86.9
  squeezed mode, r = 105.9: aspect e^(2r) = 10^92.0
  squeezed mode, r = 120.0: aspect e^(2r) = 10^104.2
  on |Z| = 1 with Im Z = sech s: with a^2 = Im Z (the record) the apex s = 0 is a maximum of a; with Im Z ~ a^-2 (section 5's wave-packet convention) it is a minimum of a: True
  radiation rectangle at a string-scale bounce, kT = 1e+17 GeV: A = 9.5e+32

== Referee A, unverifiable: Born's b
  b = h/(pi r0) = 7.485e-15 g cm/s (Born eq. 26 prints 7.43e-15); b c = 1.401e+08 eV = 2 hbar c/r0
